<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - May 9.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - May 9.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 05/09/97  05/02/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	     20.67     17.97     8.89	 7.73	5.3</p>
<p>West	     61.64     57.45    23.79	22.17     34.1</p>
<p>Total Canada   82.32     75.43    16.74	15.34     21.0</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 05/09/97: 232.55 bcf, 05/02/97: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 05/09/97: 259.11 bcf, 05/02/97: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
